title: v5.37.10 — README restructured around `paradigm shift` as single entry point
summary: 'Team audit + restructure. Author''s friend got confused setting up Paradigm because the README buried `paradigm shift` at line 218, pushed a 6-command Quick Start chain, dead-ended readers at `.purpose` with no example, and threw 20+ jargon terms before the first runnable command. Nora (ftux) simulated first-time user and produced friction report. Architect wrote restructure proposal with full `shift` overload catalog. Reviewer resolved open question (shift IS a legitimate first-install entry — shift.ts:147-178 invokes initCommand when no .paradigm/ exists). Builder rewrote README. Nora re-audit: ship-with-minor-edits, then ship-it after 3 polish edits.'
