    decision: '`paradigm shift` frames as THE single entry point in the README'
    rationale: Reviewer verified shift handles fresh-install via initCommand call when .paradigm/ is absent — no rename or command change needed
  - id: d2
    decision: Alternative install paths (script, manual, Claude Code plugin) collapsed into <details> blocks under primary npm install
    rationale: Nora flagged three-install-path paralysis as high-severity friction; npm is canonical default
  - id: d3
    decision: Audit artifacts (ftux reports, reviews) committed to git
    rationale: Preserves team audit trail; future README audits can compare against this baseline
learnings:
  - The memory note `paradigm shift guarantees 31 files/directories` is outdated — actual count is 36 (verified by grep on shift-files.ts manifest). Proposal initially claimed 37. Will update memory.
  - 'Nora''s simulation-integrity rule (user-facing surfaces only, never source code) is load-bearing: her confusion IS the data. Letting her peek at source would have corrupted the audit.'
  - When an orchestrator defaults to the wrong team (it suggested `security` for a README audit), explicitly override with the agents list. Triggers matched 'audit' but semantic context was docs UX.
  - Two-pass Nora loop (audit → builder implements → re-audit) caught 3 partial-fixes (signals/gates undefined at first use, `.purpose` lacking a narrative payoff, MCP acronym unexpanded) that would have shipped if we trusted stage 1 findings alone.
